Z||000014||cobra427||05-10-2000||01:22 AM||||oreif,<BR>you are correct in saying that the bore size of the 89 3.1 G/P is the same as the 2.8 and the cranks are different by a margin of .320<BR>in the stroke. But the difference is not made up in the rod, it is made up in the placement of the pin in the piston.The rods are the same lenght through out the 2.8-3.4.<BR>To get the 3.4L, you use the 3.1L crank and just bore it out, using the same old rods.||||reg||1
